# Swift Market LLC environment conventions
# No runtime variables are currently required by application code.
# SMTP names are documented below; values and other provider configuration remain TBF
# (To Be Finalized) until the relevant integration is approved.
# Only the disabled SMTP flag and confirmed non-secret recipient have values.
# Credentials and unverified SMTP settings are documented, never fabricated.
# .env.example must never contain secrets.
#
# Secrets must never use the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables are browser-visible and exposed/inlined at build time;
# their built values do not become private when deployment settings change.
# Real credentials belong only in uncommitted environment files (for example,
# .env.local) or approved hosting secret storage.
# Keep development, preview, and production credentials/configuration separate.
#
# Future configuration categories:
# - Production site origin / public URL: TBF; use only a verified origin.
# - Enquiry/email provider server-only credentials: TBF.
# - Receiving email configuration: TBF.
# - Analytics configuration: TBF.
# - CRM integration: TBF.
# - Chatbot/support integration: TBF.
# - Spam protection: TBF.
# - Rate-limit persistence: TBF.
# - Monitoring/error reporting: TBF.
#
# Hostinger-compatible SMTP foundation (server-only; public delivery remains disabled):
ENQUIRY_SMTP_ENABLED=false
# Set only after copying verified account settings; do not guess values.
# ENQUIRY_SMTP_HOST
# ENQUIRY_SMTP_PORT
# ENQUIRY_SMTP_SECURITY — tls (implicit TLS) or starttls (mandatory upgrade)
# ENQUIRY_SMTP_USER
# ENQUIRY_SMTP_PASSWORD — secret; never populate this example
# ENQUIRY_SMTP_FROM — owner-verified sender mailbox; not inferred from recipient
# Owner-confirmed recipient only; this does not establish sending credentials.
ENQUIRY_RECIPIENT=info@swiftmarketllc.com
# Enabling SMTP configuration does NOT enable public enquiry submission.
